Ipv6 Configuration addresses (EUI-64) :

		* EUI ---> Extended Unique Identifier

		* (Modified) EUI-64 is a method of converting a MAC address (48 bits) into a 64-bit interface identifier

		* This interface identifier can then become the 'Host Portion' of a /64 IPv6 address

		* How to convert the MAC address :

			1. Divide the MAC address in Half
		
				ex: 152A 4586 90BE -----> 152A 45 | 86 90BE

			2. Insert <FFFE> in the middle

				ex: 152A 45FF FE86 90BE

			3. Invert the 7th bit (0 become 1 | 1 become 0)
				
				ex : 152A 45FF FE86 90BE
				     ||
			  4 Bits <--- ---> 8 Bits ( the seventh bits leave in here
				      |
			   	      |	  
				      Convert it to Binary to get the seventh bit 5.

				      5 in binary is 0101
						     567 ----> 0 is the seventh bit ( invert it to 1 ), as result 0101 become 0111 (0111 = 7)
	
				152A 45FF FE86 90BE becomes 172A 45FF FE86 90BE after the convergent

